=== Generated Answer (model draft; check against evidence) ===
The Transformer scales the dot products in attention by 1/√dk to counteract the effect that, for large values of dk, the dot products grow large in magnitude, pushing the softmax function into regions where it has extremely small gradients [2]. The paper notes that additive attention outperforms dot product attention without scaling for larger values of dk, while for small values of dk the two mechanisms perform similarly [2]. Additionally, dot-product attention is much faster and more space-efficient in practice than additive attention, since it can be implemented using highly optimized matrix multiplication code, even though the two are similar in theoretical complexity [4].
